WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.110
Stan Uris is probably the most underutilized
character in both movie adaptations of It,

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.650
but in the novel, there’s a lot more to
help us understand his character.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.720
Stick around to the end of this video to find
out why.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.400
Today’s lesson is sponsored by Infertility
TV.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.060
Hello, welcome, welcome.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.060
You may be seated.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.980
They say it’s the quiet ones you have to
watch out for and Stephen King’s It definitely

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.460
embraces that concept with characters like
Patrick Hockstetter and Stan “the man”

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.460
Uris.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.160
My name is Rabbi CZsWorld and today on Horror
History we’re going to Sunday School, but

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.340
we may not be keeping it Kosher.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.020
[Horror History]

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.940
Stan is one of the seven Loser’s Club members
who battle against It, the creature looming

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.790
in the sewers of Derry, Maine.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.450
Like most of his friends, he grows up to be
quite successful, but despite his best efforts,

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.450
he and his wife are never able to have a baby.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.730
So for this episode I’m partnering with
Infertility TV - the YouTube channel dedicated

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.530
to helping you beat infertility.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:01.110
Each week, Infertility TV uploads a new video
with science-based tips from a board certified

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:05.579
fertility expert to help you and your partner
maximize your chances for getting pregnant.

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:09.200
So if you or someone you know is having trouble
like Stan did, click the link in the description

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.579
to subscribe to Infertility TV today -- it’s
like having a fertility specialist in your

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:14.600
phone.

00:01:17.529 --> 00:01:22.700
Donald Uris and Andrea Bertoli married young,
in their early 20s and in 1946 they would

00:01:22.709 --> 00:01:24.700
give birth to their only son and name him
Stanley.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.919
Stan had a Jewish upbringing, but unlike the
2017 movie adaptation of It where Stan is

00:01:29.919 --> 00:01:34.140
the son of a Rabbi, the Uris’s aren’t
particularly orthodox, they don’t keep Kosher

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.060
and don’t attend the synagogue very often.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.840
But that doesn’t stop the bullies in town
from picking on him because of his religion.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.099
When Stan was 8, Henry washed his face with
snow until it bled and Stan was crying hysterically.

00:01:45.099 --> 00:01:48.009
Each member of the Losers Club was picked
on by Henry Bowers because they had something

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:51.600
about them that made them different, but these
differences are also what made them gel as

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.600
a group.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.499
However -- Stan is a bit of different case.

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:57.429
Bowers may have singled him out due to his
religious beliefs, but I think what makes

00:01:57.429 --> 00:02:00.549
him a part of the Losers Club is his introverted
personality.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:03.069
This even comes across in the way the book
is written.

00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:06.349
Throughout the novel, each of the other 6
Losers Club members have moments where they

00:02:06.349 --> 00:02:10.500
are retelling their own story, but Stan keeps
everything to himself, we only learn more

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.260
about his story later on from the perspective
of his wife.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.909
He tends to keep things to himself, which
I see as him taking on a huge load of emotional

00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:20.569
stress and never really releasing it by opening
up to his friends about it.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:24.540
For this reason, he develops some of his own
coping mechanisms, that are apparent throughout

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.540
his story.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.790
There are many coping mechanisms recognized
by psychologists, and we can use them to follow

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.840
Stan’s breakdown from healthy to unhealthy
ways of dealing with his trauma.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.840
Stan has a close relationship with his father,
who shared his own passion of birdwatching

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.840
with his son.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.530
Together, they would often go to Memorial
Park to watch birds.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.459
This was a great spot because the War Memorial
statue in this park had once been damaged

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:48.250
in a storm and replaced with a birdbath for
budgetary reasons.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.890
Donald gave his son a gift to help him identify
some of the bird species.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:55.780
It was a book called MK Handy’s Guide to
North American Birds.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.340
Stan treasured this book and often brought
it with him whenever he went out.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.090
One day, Stan went to Memorial Park to go
birdwatching.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.469
On this occasion his father did not accompany
him.

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:09.030
He heard a loud noise come from the Standpipe,
the big water storage structure -- a landmark

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.030
of Derry.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.870
The Standpipe used to be a popular location,
there was a walkway near the top that families

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.120
would frequent to look out over the town and
a walkway over the water known as The Gallery.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.499
In 1930, some kids fell from the Gallery into
the water during the night, and had nothing

00:03:22.499 --> 00:03:24.379
to hold onto and no way to climb out.

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:28.549
They were found drowned the next morning,
and the town council locked up the Standpipe

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:30.590
and did away with letting families visit.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:34.600
That’s why Stan found it strange that the
noise he had heard at the Standpipe’s base

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.400
looked to be a padlocked door that had been
blown off.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.719
He looked inside to see a narrow set of stairs
in the dark and he could hear carnival music

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:43.370
echoing off the metallic walls.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.069
He took one step inside.

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:49.150
The music got louder and more horrifying as
squishy footsteps approached him.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:53.300
Stan, a man of logic, called out to the footsteps,
asking who was there.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.040
A voice replied to him and said, “the dead
ones.”

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.140
He realized that the door, which has seemed
to be destroyed, was now locked shut behind

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.140
him and he was trapped.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.609
They told him, “you’ll float too”.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:07.599
The footsteps continued to approach, and Stan’s
only coping mechanism is to hold out his bird

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:11.159
book and scream out the names of as many bird
species as he could think of.

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:15.450
The door behind him opened with a scream and
he fell back onto the outside grass, but before

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:20.280
he ran, he saw the purplish black jeans, small
orange pom-poms and a white gloved hand beckoning

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.040
him in the dark, along with the kids who drowned
in the Standpipe.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.139
So in this instance, Stan is faced with would
I would consider to be maybe the scariest

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:32.940
thing that any of the Losers Club members ever encountered,
and he turns to the first coping mechanism,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:33.940
escape.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.319
By focusing on his passion, Birdwatching,
he takes himself out of the moment, he basically

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:41.780
redirects his fear of It, making him a less
attractive target, and also possibly hurting

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.780
It.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.819
In June of 1958, his friend Richie Tozier
brought him along to help the Losers Club

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:50.470
build a dam in the Barrens, and they all immediately
became friends.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.110
Stan and Ben discover that they had the same
class together in 2nd grade, but Stan was

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.370
so quiet back then, he never said anything.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:00.110
They end up getting in trouble for building
the dam with a cop named Mr. Nell, since it

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.550
caused issues with the water systems in town.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:06.340
Each one of the boys stepped forward to admit
some responsibility until Stan was the only

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.660
one left, and then he too claimed to be in
on it.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:12.840
This is a small detail, but may be an early
clue towards Stan’s reluctance to be in

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.270
on any of the Club’s conflicts.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:18.050
He’s peer pressured again when they make
the promise at the end of that summer.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:21.440
Later that June, when some of the other kids
go to see the werewolf movie, Stan has to

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:25.830
stay home and do chores all weekend because
he destroyed a window while playing flying-saucer

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.090
with a plate -- to which I have to say, that
sounds 100% worth it!

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.449
So Stan is basically grounded for a couple
weeks and he shows back up around the time

00:05:32.449 --> 00:05:37.060
that Beverly is telling the boys her story
about her encounter with it: the bloody bathroom

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.060
sink in her apartment.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.949
It was Stan’s idea for all of them to go
back and clean things up, and after doing

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:46.490
so they bring the bloody rags to the laundromat
to clean them, where Stan also offers his

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.990
50 cents to run the machines.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:52.120
During this time, Ben tells of some of the
other boys’ encounters with It, but Stan

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.639
is reluctant to talk about his.

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:57.509
He would eventually tell the story about what
happened at the Standpipe, but tells the others

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:58.819
he believed it was a dream.

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:02.889
This is the next coping mechanism: denial,
and it’s one that he uses more often than

00:06:02.889 --> 00:06:06.129
any of the others, because he didn’t want
to believe that they were in danger, and by

00:06:06.129 --> 00:06:08.729
going into denial, he felt he didn’t have
to accept it.

00:06:08.729 --> 00:06:12.580
When Eddie suggests they go to the police,
Stan is the most realistic about their situation.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.169
“Right,” Stan said.

00:06:14.169 --> 00:06:15.780
“Dead kids in the Standpipe.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.789
Blood that only kids can see, not grownups.

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:19.230
Clowns walking on the Canal.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.870
Balloons that blow against the wind.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:21.870
Mummies.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:22.870
Lepers under porches.

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:26.150
Chief Borton’ll laugh his bum off . . . and
then stick us in the loony bin.”

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.220
This is Stan trying to distance himself from
the group, not because he doesn’t love them,

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:33.300
but because he is the most afraid of It out
of any of them, and he doesn’t know how

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.070
to properly deal with these emotions.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:38.320
But the following month, he’d be forced
to come to terms with the situation when he

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:42.720
experiences something so terrifying that hits
an absolute breaking point.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:53.500
On July 3rd, 1958, Stan and the other members
of the Losers Club came to the aid of Mike

00:06:53.509 --> 00:06:57.840
Hanlon by fighting off Henry Bowers and his
thugs in the apocalyptic rock fight.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.500
As Stan saw everyone gathering rocks, he had
to press his lips together in order to have

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.470
the courage to stay and fight.

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:06.910
Stan ended up helping in the barrage of rocks
that knocked Henry to the floor by nailing

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:07.910
him in the shin.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:11.520
When Henry had been driven away, Stan invited
him to shoot off firecrackers with them, and

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.030
Mike ended up joining the club, becoming the
7th and final member.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.630
After this quarrel, the Losers create their
own clubhouse in order to hide out from Henry

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:19.729
when necessary.

00:07:19.729 --> 00:07:23.419
Mike tells his new friends about his encounter
with one of the forms of It, a giant bird

00:07:23.419 --> 00:07:26.970
that had attacked him at the remains of the
old ironworks, and based on the description

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:30.680
of the bird, Stan thinks it’s a species
that’s only been known to exist in South

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:35.379
America, causing him to go pale, especially
when Mike tells about how big it was.

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:38.930
Stan is also the one to suggest that now that
Mike has shared the story with them, they’d

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.879
all be able to see it, which may have been
key in their eventual battle with the bird

00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:44.659
form in the sewers of Derry.

00:07:44.659 --> 00:07:48.409
Stan and Beverly go into town to get the hinges
needed to complete their clubhouse’s door,

00:07:48.409 --> 00:07:52.139
and after the construction is complete, on
July 6th, Mike brought his father’s photo

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:54.130
album to the Barrens to show his friends.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:58.180
The album had been used to document some historical
photographs from Derry’s history, and was

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.940
filled with subtle appearances by Pennywise.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:06.000
They land of one photo of Derry that comes
to life, and Pennywise dances and flips around

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.000
the page.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.050
Then he runs up to a lamppost in the foreground
and speaks directly to the losers.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:15.409
The plastic slot that the photo is cased in
bulges out towards them as Pennywise cycles

00:08:15.409 --> 00:08:19.780
through many of his forms, including the dead
boys that Stan had seen in the Standpipe.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:24.280
Remember, Stan had been finding ways to suppress
his fear of it until this point, telling himself

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.069
each episode was a dream or hallucination,
and he tries to do the same thing here.

00:08:28.069 --> 00:08:32.510
He goes into a manic episode, snatches up
the book and slams it shut, then holds it

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.850
closed on the ground while yelling the word
“no” over and over.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:39.700
The others force him to admit that he saw
the same thing they all saw, another example

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.450
of his subjection to peer pressure, but when
he finally does agree that what he saw was

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:47.210
real, he is able to smile and crack a joke
about Bill’s stutter, because sharing his

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:51.530
fear with his friends is the healthy response
that Stan should have been using all along.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:55.380
Humor is also one of the coping mechanisms
considered to be an adaptive mechanism; a

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.380
healthy response.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:59.980
Bill, however, still senses some hysteria
in Stan, which tells me that he still has

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:01.360
some demons locked away.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:05.350
The Losers decide to conduct a smoke hole
ceremony, which is Indian ritual where they

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.690
would sit around in a smoke hole and breath
in the fumes until they had a vision that

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.270
was supposed to help them.

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:13.880
Someone had to stay up top to pull out whoever
passed out, and Richie thought that Eddie

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.490
or Stan would be quick volunteers.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.160
“Eddie said nothing.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.650
Stan stood pale and thoughtful and silent.”

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:23.670
However, when the smoky air started to get
heavy, Stan was the first one to climb out

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:27.420
of the clubhouse, perhaps a foreshadowing
of him being unable to deal with the pressure

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.720
when It comes back in 1985, where he is also
the first one out.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:36.070
Closer to the end of that month, after Eddie's
arm is broken by Henry Bowers and his friends,

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.730
Stan joins the others in visiting Eddie in
the hospital, and Stan signs his cast across

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:40.750
Eddie’s wrist.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:44.760
Not sure if that’s a sign of things to come
for Stan, or just coincidence.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:48.540
Stan was also there when the Losers investigated
Beverly’s claims of having seen It kill

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.580
one of the bullies, Patrick Hockstetter.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:54.600
When they arrive, they discover a note left
by Pennywise in blood that reads, “Stop

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.200
now before I kill you all.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.120
A word to the wise from your friend Pennywise.”

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.960
So I got a digital copy of the book, and
looking at it on the screen like this makes

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.600
it look very much like it was written by a
fourth grader in MS Paint.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.180
But anyway, this sends Bill into a frenzy
of anger and crying, and Stan has to grab

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.420
him by the arm to prevent him from hurting
himself.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:15.950
This is where they all silently agree to help
Bill avenge his little brother.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:20.140
On July 23rd, the Losers go to Bill’s house
to make silver slugs that Beverly would later

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.190
shoot out of the slingshot at Pennywise.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:25.710
To fool Bill’s parents, they act like they
are playing Monopoly, and Stan, who would

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.930
later become a rich accountant, was the winner.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:32.940
Two days later, on July 25th, the seven of
them turned up at 29 Neibolt Street to confront

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.070
Pennywise.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:37.420
Stan brought with his North American Birds
guide in case he needed to protect himself

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:38.420
like he did before.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:42.420
They come across a corridor where the wallpaper
animates in a horrifying way and the room

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:45.790
shrinks in on them, causing Stan to cover
his eyes and scream.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:49.400
Bill punches up through where the ceiling
appears to be to prove the room is not as

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:53.670
it seems and prove to the Losers that if they
don’t believe in It’s manipulations, it

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:54.670
can’t hurt them.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.781
Stan, however, argues that someone like him
wouldn’t have been able to do that, Bill

00:10:57.781 --> 00:11:01.360
was only able to because he was fighting for
his brother, but Bill reminds him that he

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.290
already has, he did the same thing at the
Standpipe.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:08.170
Richie asks him if he’s a man or if he’s
a mouse, to which Stan says “I must be a

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:11.180
man, so far as I know, mice don’t shit their
pants.”

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:15.250
Stan once again uses humor to diffuse the
situation and doing so actually physically

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.400
deters It, Ben has the feeling that the house
is literally pulling away from them as they

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.400
laugh.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.760
After the fight with Pennywise in the bathroom,
where Beverly drives it back down into the

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:28.170
sewers with the slingshot, Stan cracks yet
another joke, but the happy times only last

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:32.480
so long with the final confrontation of the
summer looming in the near future.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:44.640
Two weeks go by before the day arrives, the
day that seven children in Maine join hands

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.280
to make a promise, a promise that would get
two of them killed 27 years later.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.980
It starts innocently enough.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.710
Stan is out in town getting popsicles with
Richie Tozier and Eddie Kaspbrak, and the

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:58.050
three boys are having a discussion about how
Stan doesn’t keep Kosher.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:01.860
They end up running into Bill, then Mike,
before crossing paths with a panting Beverly

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.320
Marsh and Ben Hanscom.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:07.670
They were being chased by the bullies, apparently
Henry Bowers had snapped and was now doing

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:08.670
It’s bidding.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:12.810
It was time for their big showdown with the
show clown, and Ben led them to the pumping

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.540
station where the seven of them would climb
down into the sewers, all while being chased

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.010
by Bowers and company.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:21.620
Because they were being followed, Stan, who
was the most afraid of It out of everybody,

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:25.270
was once again forced to stay with the group
and he was hitting new levels of anxiety.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:29.520
While traveling through one of the pipes,
something splashes nearby, and Stan screams

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:30.680
and bursts into tears.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:34.680
They light a match and discover it’s the
dead body of Patrick Hockstetter, which It

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:37.070
had dragged into the sewers to feast on.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:40.950
As they navigated, each one of the kids realized
the sewer smell was being replaced by the

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:45.330
smell of their own fears, and for Stan, that
was an awful memory from his early childhood.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:49.600
“It smelled like clay mixed with oil and
made him think of an eyeless, mouthless demon

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:53.500
called the Golem, a clay man that renegade
Jews were supposed to have raised in the Middle

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.500
Ages.”

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:58.550
Horror movie fans may remember one of the
very first horror films ever made, the 1920

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:01.060
German Expressionism picture titled The Golem.

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:06.280
Stan simply could not deal with being this
uncomfortable, terrified, wet, lost, and filthy.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:10.360
The group is attacked by It, this time in
the form of a giant eyeball with tentacles.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:14.400
Then, they reach an area that somehow resembles
a cathedral and light seems to be coming from

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:15.470
out of the walls.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:19.570
This is where the giant bird Mike had seen
makes a return at dives at them.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.550
Stan, the bird spotter, was literally the
first to spot it.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:25.750
It swoops in and scratches Eddie, ripping
his shirt in doing so.

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:29.500
Mike took his buck knife and cut the bird’s
talons as it came in to attack Eddie again,

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:32.600
and in retaliation, the bird left a long cut
on Mike’s arm.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.381
He dropped the knife and it disappeared into
the dark.

00:13:35.381 --> 00:13:38.310
The bird came back for them, and now Eddie
and Mike were defenseless.

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.390
This is where Stan had his bravest moment.

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:44.390
He steps forward in front of his friends and
screams out, proclaiming his belief in several

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:47.630
different bird species that he knows from
his book, despite the fact that he’s never

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.010
personally seen them.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:52.690
But then he calls out, “But I don’t believe
in you, so get the heck out of here!”

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:56.990
With that, the bird disappeared into the dark,
allowing them to continue onto the spider’s

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:57.990
lair.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:01.320
When Stan first saw the spider, he shrieked
like a baby, but when Bill engaged in the

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.880
metaphysical battle with It, Stan understood
that the Ritual of Chud had begun.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:09.890
After Bill had driven It away, he sensed a
feeling of doubt on Stan’s face, unsure

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:12.170
that they had really finished it off for good.

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:15.850
After making it out of the sewers alive, Bill
asks the others to make a promise.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:20.060
Stan finds a discarded Coke bottle and smashes
it open on a rock, and uses the shards to

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:23.519
cut each of their palms so that they can initiate
a blood oath.

00:14:23.519 --> 00:14:27.640
Stan makes a joke about cutting his wrists
instead, a definite foreshadowing of his eventual

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:28.640
death.

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:32.440
The seven make the pact, that if it should
ever return they would come back to defeat

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:33.640
it once more.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.250
In the years that followed, the Losers would
one by one leave Derry.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:41.480
Stan was a very good student, and secured
a scholarship to New York State University.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:45.500
One night he went along with a friend to attend
a sorority party at another school, and it

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:49.270
was there where he was introduced to Patricia
Blum and the two quickly fell in love.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:52.010
By Spring, the two were engaged at the age
of 22.

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:55.870
Stan’s parents criticized his marriage,
despite the fact that they, too, had married

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.060
extremely young.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:00.550
Patty is working to get a job as a teacher,
and Stan recommends that she apply for this

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:01.780
job in Atlanta.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:06.440
She gets it, and although the pay is not good,
the Urises move from New York to Georgia.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.480
In August of 1972, Stan and Patty were married.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:11.860
L'CHIAM!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:16.430
Stan starts by getting a job driving a bakery
truck for $100 per week, but in November he

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.600
got a job at a tax preparation company called
H&amp;R Block where he would make $150.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:25.310
This doesn’t sound like much, but when that
figure is adjusted for inflation to 2019,

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.850
it comes out at over $900.

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:33.200
Their combined income was over $17,000 a year,
or roughly over $100,000 in 2019.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:37.820
In 1973, they decided to say good-bye to the
birth control pills to try to start a family,

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:40.430
but no baby came during the next two years.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:44.550
Then in 1975, Stanley quit his job to start
his own accounting firm.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:49.080
In 1979, Stan and Patty moved to a suburb
called Traynor, where a company called Corridor

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:52.490
Video… no, not them, that’s Corridor Digital…

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:56.490
Corridor Video actually dealt with literal
videotapes, merch link in description, they

00:15:56.490 --> 00:16:00.860
moved onto a piece of land nearby and turned
into a huge client for Stan and eventually

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:05.380
earned him a full-time position at the company,
making $30,000 a year, but more importantly

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:09.550
putting Stan in contact with some of the richest
and most powerful men in Atlanta, who I can

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:13.330
only imagine are Ted Turner, Hank Aaron, Jeff
Foxworthy and the magician.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:17.130
As their income continued to grow, they focused
more of their attention on trying to have

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:20.880
kids and went to visit a fertility specialist
in Atlanta who told them there were no physical

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.750
problems preventing them from conceiving.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:27.340
By 1983, Stan was making six figures, which
when adjusted for inflation is equal to over

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:30.060
a quarter of a million dollars a year in 2019.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:34.340
Okay, that’s enough math here in the Horror
History classroom, the point is that Stan

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.420
was finally making the kind of money that
Bill teased him about during that Monopoly

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:42.300
game, and other than their unexplained infertility,
Stan had a very happy and comfortable life.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:47.080
That all changed in an instant on the evening
of May 28th, 1985.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:59.040
There were only two members of the Losers
Club who didn’t block Derry and the killing

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:03.100
spree that occurred there from Fall 1957 through
the end of the Summer in 1958 from their memories.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:07.740
The first was Mike Hanlon, and that’s only
because he never left town.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:09.409
The other was Stanley Uris.

00:17:09.409 --> 00:17:13.809
Perhaps Stan took on so much emotional damage
having gone up against the dead boys in the

00:17:13.809 --> 00:17:17.509
Standpipe, the image of the clown in the photo
album, the giant bird in the sewers and the

00:17:17.509 --> 00:17:22.319
interdimensional spider in the sanctum, that
he was simply unable to let his guard down

00:17:22.319 --> 00:17:24.260
in the 27 years that followed.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:28.189
Two weeks before the call that changed everything,
Stan had discovered that his old childhood

00:17:28.189 --> 00:17:32.610
pal Bill Denbrough was a very successful author,
and Stan’s wife had begun reading one of

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:33.610
his books.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:37.049
When Stan picks up the phone on May 28th,
he’s also able to remember his old buddy

00:17:37.049 --> 00:17:41.390
Mike Hanlon, but he almost immediately goes
quiet, which I see as the realization that

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:44.009
there could only be one reason that Mike was
calling.

00:17:44.009 --> 00:17:45.789
It had returned.

00:17:45.789 --> 00:17:49.559
Over the course of this lesson, I’ve discussed
a variety of Stan’s coping mechanisms.

00:17:49.559 --> 00:17:53.730
There are positive ones, known as adaptive
coping mechanisms, these include support,

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:57.180
like when Stan’s friends are there for him
and they talk about the issue; or humor, like

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.590
when Stan makes a joke to diffuse tension.

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:04.000
Then there are maladaptive coping mechanisms,
the negative ones; like escape, when Stan

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.160
takes his mind to another place, such as his
birds; or numbing, like when he tries to drown

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:09.769
out the horrors happening around him.

00:18:09.769 --> 00:18:15.360
But there’s one maladaptive mechanism that
Stan seemingly has not tried yet: Self Harm.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.980
At 7PM, Stan decides to take a bath.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:22.370
After some time behind the locked door, Stan
was unresponsive, so Patty found the spare

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.760
keys and unlocked the door to find she was
already too late.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:29.600
The word IT was written on the side of the
bathtub in Stan’s blood.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:33.720
Stan was intelligent, but often quiet and
out of his group of friends, he had the most

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:38.120
trouble learning to deal with the terrors
that they encountered in the summer of 1958

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.789
at the hands of Pennywise.

00:18:39.789 --> 00:18:44.000
For these reasons, the trauma he endured stuck
with him in his adult years in a way that

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:48.440
none of the others would relate to and ultimately
it ended up being his downfall.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:51.059
That concludes today’s lesson on Stan Uris.

00:18:51.059 --> 00:18:53.480
This has been another episode of Horror History.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.960
Your homework is to let me know in the comments
who I should analyse next episode and click

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:01.330
the playlist on the left to see Infertility
TV’s analysis on how Black Widow, from the

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:02.820
Avengers could have gotten pregnant.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:07.530
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, RING that deathbell for

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:10.809
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:19:10.809 --> 00:19:12.850
Assuming we both survive.

